", who: \"Antivirus\", amount: \"$16.5M\", title: \"Avast · sold the browsing of the people it protected\", body: \"The FTC found that Avast, while promising to block tracking, sold detailed, re-identifiable browsing data to more than 100 third parties through its subsidiary Jumpshot between 2014 and 2020. It is banned from selling browsing data for advertising. Avast disagrees with the characterisation of the facts.\", src: \"FTC · FEB 22, 2024\", url: S.ftcAvast }, { year: \"2025\", who: \"Apple\", amount: \"$95M\", title: \"Siri · recordings without \\\"Hey Siri\\\"\", body: \"Court-approved settlement in Lopez v. Apple: the plaintiffs alleged that Siri recorded conversations without intentional activation and that human contractors reviewed them. Apple paid without admitting wrongdoing.\", src: \"US DISTRICT COURT N.D. CAL. · 2025\", url: S.apple }, { year: \"2024\", who: \"Security\", amount: \"8.5M\", title: \"CrowdStrike · a faulty update took down millions of PCs\", body: \"On July 19, 2024 an update to the CrowdStrike Falcon security software caused blue screens on about 8.5 million Windows devices, according to Microsoft. Airports, hospitals and banks ground to a halt. It was not an attack: it was the guardian itself.\", src: \"MICROSOFT · JUL 20, 2024\", url: S.crowdstrike }], rows: [{ app: \"This PC\", dest: \"update.example-os.com\", vol: \"expected\", ok: true }, { app: \"Phone A\", dest: \"ads.example-net.com\", vol: \"advertising\", ok: false }, { app: \"TV\", dest: \"metrics.example-tv.com\", vol: \"telemetry\", ok: false }, { app: \"Phone B\", dest: \"g.whatsapp.net\", vol: \"expected\", ok: true }, { app: \"Tablet\", dest: \"trk.example-affil.io\", vol: \"tracker\", ok: false }, { app: \"This PC\", dest: \"time.example-ntp.org\", vol: \"expected\", ok: true }, { app: \"Phone A\", dest: \"dns.example-resolver.com\", vol: \"unknown\", ok: false }, { app: \"TV\", dest: \"cdn.example-video.com\", vol: \"expected\", ok: true }] };\n    const shown = st